Add admin gating for library and vector index maintenance

Only users listed in the DASHBOARD_ADMINS env var (comma-separated
AbbVie usernames, case-insensitive) can now trigger writes to the
shared library_index.json and library_vectors.npz. Non-admins see the
same data but with Sync, Rebuild, Force-rescan, Organize, Build-index,
and Full-rebuild buttons hidden, plus an explanatory banner naming
who to ask.

This is a UI guardrail, not a security boundary — anyone with shell
access can still edit the files directly. The point is to eliminate
the multi-user race conditions on those shared files by ensuring only
one person can trigger writes.

If DASHBOARD_ADMINS is unset (default), the current user is treated as
admin so local development still works. On CML, set it via
Project Settings -> Environment Variables.

New file: auth.py — current_user(), is_admin(), admin_contact().
Current user is read from CDSW_USER, HADOOP_USER_NAME, USERNAME, or USER.
